<p>“You’re going to do great,” I said.</p>
<p>But my son seemed tentative.</p>
<p>“Dad?” he said. “I don’t feel ready.”</p>
<p>I sighed.</p>
<p>It can be so hard for me to remember: he’s not just my intern and temporary CFO. He’s a boy.</p>
<p>I asked him if he thought Mark Zuckerberg felt ready when he launched Facebook. I asked him if he thought Elon Musk felt ready when he took over Twitter. I asked him if he thought Steve Ballmer felt ready when he made the daunting move from tech leadership into sports ownership.</p>
